  "final_text": "Both objects exist in Kibana 9.5.5: the dashboard and the enabled rule.\n\n**Data exploration** (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, 14,074 documents)\n- `response` holds the status code as a string. The codes are 200 (12,832), 404 (801) and 503 (441). 503 is the only 5xx code present.\n- Other useful fields: `bytes`, `clientip`, `url`, `geo.*`, `agent`, `extension`, `machine.os`.\n- The timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, so part of the data is in the future relative to today (2026-10-12).\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-fbf5c696 Web logs overview\"** (ID `389e814c-f819-465c-891d-6921834603f6`)\nFour ES|QL-backed panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- 5xx responses (count of codes 500\u2013599)\n- Bytes transferred (sum of `bytes`)\n- Responses by status code (pie)\n\n**Rule: \"EFF-fbf5c696 5xx spike\"** (ID `33effa5b-94f8-4a9a-874a-ea46049b6bf0`)\n- Type: index threshold, on `kibana_sample_data_logs` by `timestamp`.\n- Filter: `response.keyword >= \"500\" and response.keyword <= \"599\"`.\n- Count over the last 5 minutes, `>` 10, checked every 1 minute.\n- Enabled. Its last run succeeded with status `ok`.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- The dashboard time range is `now-1y` to `now+1y` so the sample data falls inside it.\n- The 5xx filter uses a string range on the keyword field. That is correct for three-digit codes, but it is lexicographic.\n- The rule has no actions, so it will not send notifications. Tell me if you want an email or Slack connector attached.\n- The public API has no raw search endpoint, so I ran the exploration queries through Kibana's internal search endpoint. The API key only needs to read the data for that.\n\n**One thing to check:** the rule only fires if more than 10 5xx requests fall in the last 5 minutes. I did not check whether any documents fall in that window. Given the future-dated sample timestamps, it may not fire until those timestamps arrive.",
